   * **Balancing phase** (once it is close to the upright) – a gentle proportional‑derivative (PD) controller is enough and keeps the cost low.  

The two‑phase idea is a classic solution for the classic “inverted pendulum swing‑up” problem and explains why the “only‑angle” run performed better: it unintentionally produced larger torques when the pendulum was far from the upright, but it still used the same aggressive torque when the pole was already near the goal, causing overshoot and extra cost.

