## 5️⃣  What to try next (if further tuning is needed)

| What to tune | Why it matters | Suggested range |
|--------------|----------------|-----------------|
| `θ_sw` (switch angle) | Larger value gives more time for the swing‑up controller, smaller value reduces overshoot before PD takes over | 0.25 – 0.35 rad |
| `Kp` / `Kd` | Controls speed vs. overshoot of the balancing controller | `Kp: 8‑12`, `Kd: 2‑3` |
| `bias` coefficient (`0.5` above) | Too large a bias can fight the energy term; too small can cause the pendulum to linger near the switching band | 0.3 – 0.7 |
| `kE` scaling factor (`5.0`) | Higher values give more aggressive energy injection, but may saturate torque early | 4 – 6 |

A simple **grid‑search** over these 4 parameters (≈ 30 – 50 trials) should quickly reveal a combination that pushes the average reward below **‑30**.

