| **Crossing the top** | As `|θ|` shrinks below 0.25 rad the controller switches to the linear mode. The `sin(θ)` term cancels gravity, the PD part damps the remaining velocity. | The pole settles quickly around θ ≈ 0 with very small ω. |
| **Balancing** | With the PD/LQR active the torque stays in the range `[-0.2, 0.2]` (usually 0). The cost per step is then ≈ ‑θ² ‑ 0.1 ω², i.e. almost zero. | The cumulative reward improves dramatically compared with the previous attempts. |

